.TH "SCCFM-CLI OBJECTS EDIT-OVERRIDE" "1" "2026-08-18" "0.39.1" "sccfm-cli objects edit-override Manual"
.SH NAME
sccfm-cli\-objects\-edit-override \- Edit the value of an existing override for...
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sccfm-cli objects edit-override
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Edit the value of an existing override for a specific target device.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-u,\fP \-\-uid TEXT
The unique identifier (UID) of the object.
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-id\fP TEXT
UID of the target device whose override to edit.  [required]
.TP
\fB\-\-override\-value\fP TEXT
The new override value (IP address, CIDR, range, or URL).  [required]
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fP [table|json]
Output format  [default: table]
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-path\fP PATH
Path to the configuration file (defaults to ~/.sccfm-cli/config.json).
